  [PASS] E1 the catalogue's own parameterisation is recovered exactly: rho_0 is a function of C200 alone and rs = V200/(10 H0 C200) with H0 = 73 km/s/Mpc, both to the table's rounding precision -- so the engine below is fitting the SAME two parameters Li fitted   (worst rms residual over the four models 0.0032 dex (table rounding is 0.005 dex))
  [PASS] E2 AND the catalogue's quoted e_rs is EXACTLY the propagation of e_V200 and e_C200 assuming they are UNCORRELATED (ratio 1.000), while the actual posterior correlation measured below is -0.90 to -0.98.  The published error bars on r_0 therefore cannot be used as an error ellipse for item 106 -- the correlation has to be re-derived, which is what the engine does   (e_rs/propagation = 1.000 worst; e_logM200/propagation = 1.002 worst)

  recomputing the (V200, C200) posterior for 4 models x 175 galaxies -- this is the slow part (~3 min)
  posteriors computed: 682 galaxy-model pairs in 37 s
