  Burkert-Flat   N=171  my sigma(logV200)/Li's = 0.90, sigma(logC200)/Li's = 0.85   |  correlation of (log rho_0, log r_0) = -0.930   DEGENERACY SLOPE = -1.74
  NFW-Flat       N=171  my sigma(logV200)/Li's = 0.93, sigma(logC200)/Li's = 0.86   |  correlation of (log rho_0, log r_0) = -0.978   DEGENERACY SLOPE = -1.46
  NFW-LCDM       N=171  my sigma(logV200)/Li's = 1.23, sigma(logC200)/Li's = 0.92   |  correlation of (log rho_0, log r_0) = -0.946   DEGENERACY SLOPE = -1.65
  caveat stated against interest: sigma(log C200) matches Li's to 0.85-0.92 for Burkert and both NFW variants but only 0.45
  for pISO, so the pISO ellipse below is probably too TIGHT and its degeneracy correction correspondingly under-applied.
  [PASS] E3 the re-derived posterior reproduces Li's own quoted parameter uncertainties to within a factor ~1.3, which is what licenses using its CORRELATION (the thing Li does not publish) as the error ellipse for items 106 and 107   (median sigma(log V200) mine/Li over the four models: [0.91 0.9  0.93 1.23])
  [PASS] E4 (bug pattern 4, checked explicitly rather than assumed) every 2x2 error ellipse used below -- in both orderings, since the (log rho_0, log r_0) matrix is transposed into (x, y) = (log r_0, log rho_0) for the regression -- is symmetric and POSITIVE DEFINITE, not merely positive on the diagonal.  An earlier item in this hunt was voided by exactly this   (682 posteriors x 3 orderings checked, 0 non-positive-definite; worst eigenvalue ratio 3.6e-06, and 5 of 2046 are thinner than 1e-4 -- those are the galaxies whose rotation curve fixes one combination of (V200, C200) and says almost nothing about the other, which is the physical situation and not a numerical failure)

======================================================================================================================
ITEM 106 -- the rho_0 - r_0 anti-correlation: is the slope -1, and is -1 free?
======================================================================================================================
  the prediction restated exactly: log rho_0 = log Sigma_M - log r_0 has slope -1 IF AND ONLY IF the product does not
  itself depend on r_0, since  d log rho_0/d log r_0 = -1 + d log(rho_0 r_0)/d log r_0.  Item 5 already measured the
  product: median 177 Msun/pc^2 for Burkert with a 0.45 dex SCATTER, so 'constant' is a statement about the median only.
  Sigma_M = a_0/(2 pi G) = 106.9 (canonical) / 129.0 (alt) Msun/pc^2.

  (a) the NAIVE slope, straight from the catalogue, every model:
      Burkert-Flat    N=162  slope -1.193 +- 0.109   residual scatter 0.440 dex
      DC14-Flat       N=162  slope -1.405 +- 0.106   residual scatter 0.537 dex
      DC14-LCDM       N=159  slope -0.888 +- 0.120   residual scatter 0.443 dex
